  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1257 PM CDT Wed Aug 19 2026\n\nGFS continues to show a few storms possible on Saturday afternoon\nacross the eastern Big Country and Heartland, although this idea\nisn't well supported by some of the other models. Starting to get\ninto the range where the CAMs will start picking it up and will\nlet that play out before adding POPs back into the forecast.\n\nOtherwise, upper ridge shows every indication of building even\nmore across West Central Texas for the weekend into next week,\nboosting temperatures even more. Will likely see highs at or above\n105 start to spread farther south into the Concho Valley and\nHeartland and that means a likely expansion of the Heat Advisory\nsouth across more of the area as we get into next week. \n\nOf note, Abilene is now sitting at 17 consecutive days of 100+\ndegree temperatures, 18 if you include today. The record for\nconsecutive 100 degree days in Abilene sits at 30 days that\ncovered virtually all of August in 1952. Given the forecast and\nthe longer range trends beyond even the official forecast, this\nrecord may well be in jeopardy.",
